## In short

The source code of Loop is open. You may read it, clone it, study it, change it,
build it yourself and run it on devices you own. What you may not do is pass it
on: no store, no TestFlight — not even your own —, no sideloading to anyone
else, no handing a compiled build to a friend, no selling it, and no presenting
yourself as the author or provider of Loop under whatever name. Loop is and
stays a product of Levo Studio. Pull requests are expressly welcome, and every
contribution is named in the credits.

This is not an open-source license in the sense of the Open Source Definition,
because it restricts distribution and commercial use. From here on the sections
apply. Where the summary and the sections disagree, the sections win.

## 1. Acceptance

Whoever exercises one of the permissions granted below accepts this license.
Whoever does not accept it has no rights in the software.

## 2. Grant of rights

Subject to the conditions and limits of this license, the licensor grants you a
worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable and non-sublicensable
right

  (a) to retrieve, read and study the source code of the software;

  (b) to reproduce, compile, build and run the software on devices that you own
      or control;

  (c) to modify the software for your own use and to build and run the modified
      version under the terms of (b); and

  (d) to make the source code available as a public fork within the narrow
      limits set out at the end of section 3, and to submit contributions under
      section 4.

No further rights are granted. Section 3 limits this grant and prevails in the
event of a conflict.

## 3. What is not permitted

Without a separate written agreement with Levo Studio, the following is
prohibited:

  (a) distributing the software or a version derived from it in any form —
      including publication in the App Store or in any other app store,
      marketplace or distribution channel, distribution via TestFlight
      including a TestFlight programme of your own, sideloading to third
      parties, and passing a compiled binary to any other person at all,
      regardless of the name used and regardless of whose developer account is
      involved;

  (b) selling, renting, leasing, sublicensing or otherwise transferring the
      software or a version derived from it for a fee or any other
      consideration;

  (c) using the software to offer a product or a service to third parties, for
      a fee or free of charge, including any hosted offering or any offering
      operated as software as a service;

  (d) incorporating the software into a commercially offered product or a
      commercially offered service;

  (e) presenting yourself as the author, publisher or provider of Loop, or
      creating that impression;

  (f) making a modified version of the software publicly available, publishing
      it or distributing it publicly; the only exceptions are the submission of
      contributions under section 4 and a public fork within the limits set out
      at the end of this section;

  (g) removing, altering or obscuring copyright, license or provenance notices
      in the software;

  (h) using the name "Loop", the mark "Levo Studio", the logo, the app icon or
      the visual design of the app for a product, a service or a version of the
      software of your own.

**Public forks.** A fork of the source code on a code-hosting platform is exempt
from (a) and (f), provided that it

  (i)   contains source code only, no compiled binary and no build ready to
        install;

  (ii)  leaves the notices under (g) unchanged and carries this license file
        unchanged; and

  (iii) serves the preparation of a contribution under section 4 or your own
        use under section 2 (b) and (c).

This exemption is limited to the fork itself. It permits no other form of
distribution, and in particular it does not permit passing a compiled binary or
an installable build to anyone.

## 4. Contributions

Contributions are welcome. Whoever has an idea that makes Loop better should
open a pull request.

  (a) Whoever submits a contribution grants Levo Studio a worldwide,
      royalty-free, irrevocable, perpetual, non-exclusive and sublicensable
      right to reproduce, modify, distribute, make publicly available and
      exploit the contribution — in the project, in the published app and in
      future versions, including versions offered for a fee.

  (b) Authorship of the contribution stays with the contributor. The grant of
      rights under (a) is not a transfer of authorship.

  (c) The contributor is named in the credits of the project. The rules for
      that entry are in the README.

  (d) Whoever submits a contribution warrants that they hold the rights
      required to do so and that the contribution does not infringe the rights
      of third parties.

  (e) Levo Studio is under no obligation to accept, adopt or publish a
      contribution.

## 5. Trademarks and design

This license grants no rights in the trademarks, signs, names, logos or product
names of Levo Studio, in particular none in the designations "Levo Studio" and
"Loop" and none in the app icon, the word-and-figure mark and the visual design
of the app.

You may not use these signs for a product, a service or a version of the
software of your own, and you may not act in a way that suggests a connection
with Levo Studio or an endorsement by Levo Studio.

Plain factual reference is permitted: you may say that your version is based on
Loop by Levo Studio.

## 6. Patents

This license grants no patent rights, neither expressly nor by implication.
Whoever initiates or knowingly supports patent proceedings asserting that the
